Translation patch: libsignal_protocol::ratchet::keys::RootKey::create_chain

Change: `derive_arrays` is replaced by a zeroed 64-byte buffer filled by `crate::crypto::hkdf_sha256(Some(&self.key), &shared_secret, b"WhisperRatchet", ..)`, then copied into two 32-byte arrays (`derive_arrays` derived 32, 32 and 0 bytes here). The `.expect("valid output length")` moves from the closure to the call. The `use libsignal_core::derive_arrays` stays, for `MessageKeys::derive_keys`.
Why: `derive_arrays` has no body in any profile. The core profile excludes it, because its zerocopy-based impls crash an Aeneas pre-pass (`aeneas-config.core.yml`), and the protocol profile has only an outside declaration for it. Without this patch, `create_chain` translates but takes both keys from that bodiless function, so nothing links them to the HKDF output.
Behaviour: identical. The same HKDF call, with the same salt, input and info, fills the same 64 bytes; bytes 0-31 become the root key and bytes 32-63 the chain key, as before, with the same `expect` message.
Relies on: protocol-crypto-hkdf_sha256.patch
Applies after: protocol-ratchet_keys-RootKey-create_chain.patch (its lines are this patch's context).

diff --git a/rust/protocol/src/ratchet/keys.rs b/rust/protocol/src/ratchet/keys.rs
--- a/rust/protocol/src/ratchet/keys.rs
+++ b/rust/protocol/src/ratchet/keys.rs
@@ -202,10 +202,15 @@
         our_ratchet_key: &PrivateKey,
     ) -> Result<(RootKey, ChainKey)> {
         let shared_secret = our_ratchet_key.calculate_agreement(their_ratchet_key)?;
-        let (root_key, chain_key, []) = derive_arrays(|bytes| {
-            crate::crypto::hkdf_sha256(Some(&self.key), &shared_secret, b"WhisperRatchet", bytes)
-                .expect("valid output length")
-        });
+        // Keep the byte splitting explicit: the extraction backend cannot translate
+        // the zerocopy-derived layout implementations used by derive_arrays.
+        let mut bytes = [0u8; 64];
+        crate::crypto::hkdf_sha256(Some(&self.key), &shared_secret, b"WhisperRatchet", &mut bytes)
+            .expect("valid output length");
+        let mut root_key = [0u8; 32];
+        let mut chain_key = [0u8; 32];
+        root_key.copy_from_slice(&bytes[..32]);
+        chain_key.copy_from_slice(&bytes[32..]);
 
         Ok((
             RootKey { key: root_key },
